  {
   "id": "D3",
   "type": "definition",
   "name": null,
   "statement": "We define the basic ring operations of addition, negation, and multiplication in the usual way. For example, $(a_1 + a_n\\sqrt{n})(b_1 + b_n\\sqrt{n}) = (a_1b_1 + na_nb_n) + (a_1b_n + a_nb_1)\\sqrt{n}$. Note that this definition only makes sense if $A$ supports these operations.",
   "origin": "paper",
   "tags": [
    "leanok",
    "lean"
   ],
   "section": "7.1 Adjoining a square root",
   "label": "def:adjoinRingOps",
   "lean_names": [
