  {
   "id": "D4",
   "type": "definition",
   "name": null,
   "statement": "We define $(a_1 + a_n\\sqrt{n})^{-1}$ as follows: \\begin{eqnarray*} \\frac{1}{a_1 + a_n\\sqrt{n}} & = & \\frac{1}{a_1 + a_n\\sqrt{n}} \\cdot \\frac{a_1 - a_n\\sqrt{n}}{a_1 - a_n\\sqrt{n}} = \\frac{a_1 - a_n\\sqrt{n}}{a_1^2 - na_n^2} \\\\ \\\\ & = & a_1(a_1^2 - na_n^2)^{-1} - a_n(a_1^2 - na_n^2)^{-1}\\sqrt{n} \\\\ \\end{eqnarray*} As long as $A$ has inverses, this is an element of $A[\\sqrt{n}]$.",
   "origin": "paper",
   "tags": [
    "leanok",
    "lean"
   ],
   "section": "7.1 Adjoining a square root",
   "label": "def:adjoinInv",
   "lean_names": [
    "AdjoinSqrt.instInv"
