  {
   "id": "D5",
   "type": "definition",
   "name": null,
   "statement": "A signed ring is a ring $A$ coupled with a function $sign : A \u2192 \\{0, 1, -1\\}$ satisfying the following properties: \\begin{itemize} \\item $sign~0 = 0$ \\item $sign~1 = 1$ \\item $sign~(ab) = (sign~a)(sign~b)$ \\item if $sign~a = 0$ then $a = 0$ \\item $sign~(-a) = -sign~a$ \\item if $sign~a \\geq 0$ and $sign~b~\\geq 0$ then $sign~(a + b) \\geq 0$ \\end{itemize}",
   "origin": "paper",
   "tags": [
    "leanok",
    "lean"
   ],
   "section": "7.1 Adjoining a square root",
   "label": "def:signedRing",
   "lean_names": [
    "SignedRing"
   ]
