   "id": "D9",
   "type": "definition",
   "name": null,
   "statement": "Given a function $f : \u03b1 \u2192 \u211d$, a \\texttt{FilteredReal f} value consists of an unevaluated value of type $\u03b1$ and a closed floating-point interval that contains $f \u03b1$. We consider two values in \\texttt{FilteredReal f} to be equal if the wrapped $\u03b1$ values are equal; the intervals are just an approximation.",
